{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc | sed -n '25,135p;300,485p'\"","aggregated_output":"    25\t\n    26\t(defn empty-registry\n    27\t  \"An empty module registry value.\"\n    28\t  []\n    29\t  {:modules {}, :effect-handlers {}})\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\t(defn- symbol->path\n    33\t  \"Split a dotted symbol into a get-in path of symbols.\n    34\t   'yin.io.file-input-stream → ['yin 'io 'file-input-stream]\"\n    35\t  [sym]\n    36\t  (mapv symbol (str/split (str sym) #\"\\.\")))\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(defn- walk-path\n    40\t  \"Descend a registry's :modules map along path, a sequence of symbols.\n    41\t\n    42\t   Namespace segments step through plain maps until the path reaches a\n    43\t   module entry (a map carrying :manifest); the remaining segments read\n    44\t   that entry's task-local lowered `:bindings` when it holds them -- a\n    45\t   linked module (yin.vm.linker.md section 8.3) -- and its `:slice`\n    46\t   otherwise, which for a host module is the host values themselves, so\n    47\t   a binding name resolves to its export.\"\n    48\t  [node path]\n    49\t  (if (seq path)\n    50\t    (if (and (map? node) (contains? node :manifest))\n    51\t      (get-in node (into [(if (contains? node :bindings) :bindings :slice)]\n    52\t                         path))\n    53\t      (when-let [child (get node (first path))]\n    54\t        (walk-path child (rest path))))\n    55\t    node))\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(defn module-entry\n    59\t  \"The registry entry of module `module-name` in `modules` (a registry's\n    60\t   `:modules` map), or nil when the dotted path reaches no module entry.\"\n    61\t  [modules module-name]\n    62\t  (let [node (reduce (fn [node seg] (when (map? node) (get node seg)))\n    63\t                     modules\n    64\t                     (symbol->path module-name))]\n    65\t    (when (and (map? node) (contains? node :manifest)) node)))\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t(defn assoc-module\n    69\t  \"Return registry with `entry` installed as module `module-name`.\"\n    70\t  [registry module-name entry]\n    71\t  (assoc-in (or registry (empty-registry))\n    72\t            (into [:modules] (symbol->path module-name))\n    73\t            entry))\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\t(defn link-module\n    77\t  \"The `linked` transition's registry update (yin.vm.linker.md sections\n    78\t   7.3 and 8.3): `registry` gains the module `manifest` names as the\n    79\t   portable encoding of acts 1 to 3 -- `{:manifest m :address a\n    80\t   :derivation d :slice {sym encoded} :stores {address snapshot} :images\n    81\t   {identity image}}` -- never lowered values. `a` is the manifest's own\n    82\t   address; `lifted` is the act-1 lift, `{:slice :stores :images}`, the\n    83\t   images being the verified origin images a receiving task attaches.\n    84\t   Each receiving task lowers the entry into its own `:bindings`.\"\n    85\t  [registry manifest derivation lifted]\n    86\t  (assoc-module registry\n    87\t                (:yin.module/name manifest)\n    88\t                {:manifest manifest,\n    89\t                 :address (jing/segment-key manifest),\n    90\t                 :derivation derivation,\n    91\t                 :slice (:slice lifted),\n    92\t                 :stores (:stores lifted),\n    93\t                 :images (:images lifted)}))\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\t(defn module-entries\n    97\t  \"Every `[name entry]` a registry value holds, the module name read back\n    98\t   from each entry's manifest.\"\n    99\t  [registry]\n   100\t  (letfn [(walk\n   101\t            [node]\n   102\t            (when (map? node)\n   103\t              (if (contains? node :manifest)\n   104\t                [[(:yin.module/name (:manifest node)) node]]\n   105\t                (mapcat walk (vals node)))))]\n   106\t    (vec (walk (:modules registry)))))\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\t(defn resolve-module\n   110\t  \"Get a value from a registry value by dotted symbol path.\n   111\t   (resolve-module r 'io)                    → the 'io registry entry\n   112\t   (resolve-module r 'io.file-output-stream) → the specific export\"\n   113\t  [registry sym]\n   114\t  (walk-path (:modules registry) (symbol->path sym)))\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t(defn register-effect-handler\n   118\t  \"Return registry with handler-fn installed for effect keyword kw.\n   119\t   Handler: (fn [state effect opts] -> {:state s :value v :blocked? bool})\"\n   120\t  [registry kw handler-fn]\n   121\t  (assoc-in (or registry (empty-registry)) [:effect-handlers kw] handler-fn))\n   122\t\n   123\t\n   124\t(defn get-effect-handler\n   125\t  \"Get the handler function for an effect keyword.\"\n   126\t  [registry kw]\n   127\t  (get (:effect-handlers registry) kw))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn list-modules\n   131\t  \"List the top-level module names in a registry value.\"\n   132\t  [registry]\n   133\t  (keys (:modules registry)))\n   134\t\n   135\t\n   300\t  (register-host-module registry 'stream stream-module stream-profiles))\n   301\t\n   302\t\n   303\t;; =============================================================================\n   304\t;; Built-in effect handlers\n   305\t;; =============================================================================\n   306\t\n   307\t;; =============================================================================\n   308\t;; `require` lowers to the linker (yin.vm.linker.md section 7)\n   309\t;; =============================================================================\n   310\t\n   311\t(defprotocol IModuleKernel\n   312\t  \"What a kernel supplies the install child and the `linked` transition\n   313\t   (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3). Every method is a pure function of a\n   314\t   VM value; the engine owns the phases, the kernel owns its coordinates.\"\n   315\t\n   316\t  (link-format\n   317\t    [vm]\n   318\t    \"`{:format kw :contract s}`: the format this kernel links, and the\n   319\t     execution contract it runs.\")\n   320\t\n   321\t  (spawn-module\n   322\t    [vm image opts]\n   323\t    \"A fresh VM of this backend with the verified `image` loaded by the\n   324\t     ordinary loader, holding nothing of `vm`'s state but its composition\n   325\t     values (primitives, stream constructor, link pair). `opts` carries\n   326\t     `:modules` (the child's module view), `:origin`, and `:ancestry`.\")\n   327\t\n   328\t  (image-identity\n   329\t    [vm image]\n   330\t    \"The identity this kernel's code space names `image` by: H, R, the\n   331\t     vector's address, or the tree's root row id.\")\n   332\t\n   333\t  (image-holds?\n   334\t    [vm image segment]\n   335\t    \"True when a closure marker's `:yin.k/segment` falls in `image`.\")\n   336\t\n   337\t  (attach-module\n   338\t    [vm image]\n   339\t    \"`vm` with `image` attached by the kernel's `attach-image` under its\n   340\t     own contract; an image already held is not attached twice.\")\n   341\t\n   342\t  (lift-closure\n   343\t    [vm closure encode]\n   344\t    \"The `:yin.k/closure` marker of `closure` in `vm`'s coordinates,\n   345\t     captured values encoded by `encode`, with `:yin.k/store-of` when the\n   346\t     closure carries one. Throws the `:yin.k/non-portable` refusal as\n   347\t     ex-data when the closure cannot be lifted.\")\n   348\t\n   349\t  (lower-closure\n   350\t    [vm marker decode]\n   351\t    \"The closure `marker` denotes in `vm`'s coordinates, captured values\n   352\t     decoded by `decode`, carrying the marker's `:yin.k/store-of`. A\n   353\t     marker of another binding discipline or format is\n   354\t     `:binding-mismatch`.\"))\n   355\t\n   356\t\n   357\t(def link-request-resource\n   358\t  \"The private resource id of the link request stream (section 6.1): the\n   359\t   writer the composition supplied. No store instruction reaches it.\"\n   360\t  :yin.link/request)\n   361\t\n   362\t\n   363\t(def link-response-resource\n   364\t  \"The private resource id of the link response stream.\"\n   365\t  :yin.link/response)\n   366\t\n   367\t\n   368\t(defn- installing?\n   369\t  [state module-name]\n   370\t  (contains? (:installs state) module-name))\n   371\t\n   372\t\n   373\t(defn- block-on\n   374\t  \"The handler outcome that parks the continuation as `entry`.\"\n   375\t  [state entry]\n   376\t  {:state (-> state\n   377\t              (update :wait-set (fnil conj []) entry)\n   378\t              (assoc :value :yin/blocked\n   379\t                     :blocked? true\n   380\t                     :halted? false)),\n   381\t   :value :yin/blocked,\n   382\t   :blocked? true})\n   383\t\n   384\t\n   385\t(defn- mint-link-id\n   386\t  \"The next link id `[origin counter]` of this task (section 7.2, step 3):\n   387\t   the task's origin tag beside its own engine counter.\"\n   388\t  [state]\n   389\t  (let [counter (or (:id-counter state) 0)]\n   390\t    [[(or (:origin state) :t0) counter]\n   391\t     (assoc state :id-counter (inc counter))]))\n   392\t\n   393\t\n   394\t(defn append-link-request\n   395\t  \"Append `entry`'s retained envelope on the link request stream. `ok`\n   396\t   moves the entry to the `:link-response` state; `full` keeps it in\n   397\t   `:link-request`, envelope verbatim, for the next poll; the terminal\n   398\t   outcomes throw, naming the outcome and the link id.\"\n   399\t  [resources entry]\n   400\t  (let [writer (get resources link-request-resource)\n   401\t        o (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! writer (:envelope entry)))]\n   402\t    (case o\n   403\t      :dao.stream/ok (-> entry\n   404\t                         (dissoc :envelope)\n   405\t                         (assoc :reason :link-response))\n   406\t      :dao.stream/full entry\n   407\t      (throw (ex-info \"Link request could not be appended\"\n   408\t                      {:outcome o, :link-id (:link-id entry)})))))\n   409\t\n   410\t\n   411\t(defn require-handler\n   412\t  \"Resolve `:module/require` (yin.vm.linker.md sections 7.2 and 8.3).\n   413\t\n   414\t   A module already in the registry value -- a host module, or one linked\n   415\t   earlier and lowered into this task -- answers now. A module installing\n   416\t   in this scheduler (section 7.3) is neither linked nor absent: the\n   417\t   requiring continuation joins that install's waiters as an `:install`\n   418\t   entry. Anything else is a miss, and a miss never throws for absence:\n   419\t   it mints a `:dao.stream/newest` cursor on the link response stream,\n   420\t   THEN builds the `:link-request` wait entry -- cursor before append, so\n   421\t   a response that lands before the entry is first polled is not skipped\n   422\t   -- and appends the envelope under the link id `[origin counter]`. On\n   423\t   `ok` the entry waits in `:link-response`; on `full` it stays in\n   424\t   `:link-request` and the poll retries it. The entry is the kernel's\n   425\t   registers plus the link fields: resource ids and plain data, never a\n   426\t   handle.\n   427\t\n   428\t   A module already on this task's install ancestry is `:require-cycle`\n   429\t   naming the chain (section 7.4): the child that asked is refused. A VM\n   430\t   composed without a link pair cannot link, so its miss fails as v1's\n   431\t   did, naming the modules it has.\"\n   432\t  [state effect {:keys [park-entry-fns]}]\n   433\t  (let [module-name (:module effect)\n   434\t        build (get park-entry-fns :module/require)\n   435\t        registers #(if build (build state effect nil) {})\n   436\t        resources (:resources state)\n   437\t        response (get resources link-response-resource)]\n   438\t    (cond\n   439\t      (some? (resolve-module (:modules state) module-name))\n   440\t      {:value module-name, :state state, :blocked? false}\n   441\t\n   442\t      (some #{module-name} (:ancestry state))\n   443\t      (throw (ex-info \"Require cycle\"\n   444\t                      {:reason :require-cycle,\n   445\t                       :module module-name,\n   446\t                       :chain (conj (vec (:ancestry state)) module-name)}))\n   447\t\n   448\t      (installing? state module-name)\n   449\t      (block-on state (assoc (registers) :reason :install :name module-name))\n   450\t\n   451\t      (not (and response (get resources link-request-resource)))\n   452\t      (throw (ex-info \"Module is not in this VM's registry\"\n   453\t                      {:module module-name,\n   454\t                       :available (vec (list-modules (:modules state)))}))\n   455\t\n   456\t      :else\n   457\t      (let [minted (stream/cursor response stream/anchor-newest)\n   458\t            _ (when-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome minted))\n   459\t                (throw (ex-info \"Link response cursor mint failed\"\n   460\t                                {:outcome (:dao.stream/outcome minted),\n   461\t                                 :module module-name})))\n   462\t            [link-id state] (mint-link-id state)\n   463\t            {:keys [format contract]} (link-format state)\n   464\t            entry (assoc (registers)\n   465\t                         :reason :link-request\n   466\t                         :name module-name\n   467\t                         :link-id link-id\n   468\t                         :envelope {:yin.link/id link-id,\n   469\t                                    :yin.link/name module-name,\n   470\t                                    :yin.link/format format,\n   471\t                                    :yin.link/contract contract}\n   472\t                         :request link-request-resource\n   473\t                         :response link-response-resource\n   474\t                         :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor minted))]\n   475\t        (block-on state (append-link-request resources entry))))))\n   476\t\n   477\t\n   478\t(defn default-registry\n   479\t  \"A registry with the built-in effect handlers and no modules.\"\n   480\t  []\n   481\t  (-> (empty-registry)\n   482\t      (register-effect-handler :module/require require-handler)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
