{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '110,170p;960,1080p;1235,1305p'\"","aggregated_output":"   110\t;; address of the module whose store their body resolves against. The\n   111\t;; positional kernels hold the running body's `:store-of` as a register,\n   112\t;; saved in every return frame and parked payload; the named kernels carry\n   113\t;; it in the lexical environment under the same key, so a closure captures\n   114\t;; it with its environment, a frame's saved environment restores it, and a\n   115\t;; halt strips it. The receiving task instantiates each module's store\n   116\t;; under `:module-stores {m {sym value}}`, never into its own `:store`.\n   117\t\n   118\t(def store-of-key\n   119\t  \"The key a closure (and, for the named kernels, an environment) carries\n   120\t   the manifest address of its module store under.\"\n   121\t  :yin.k/store-of)\n   122\t\n   123\t\n   124\t(defn env-store-of\n   125\t  \"The module store a named kernel's environment `env` runs against, or\n   126\t   nil at top level.\"\n   127\t  [env]\n   128\t  (get env store-of-key))\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn without-store-of\n   132\t  \"`env` with no module store context: what a halt leaves, so the next\n   133\t   top-level input never routes through a stale module store.\"\n   134\t  [env]\n   135\t  (if (contains? env store-of-key) (dissoc env store-of-key) env))\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\t(defn store-context\n   139\t  \"The module store the running body of `state` routes to, or nil: the\n   140\t   positional kernels' `:store-of` register, else the named kernels'\n   141\t   environment.\"\n   142\t  [state]\n   143\t  (or (:store-of state) (env-store-of (:env state))))\n   144\t\n   145\t\n   146\t(defn active-store\n   147\t  \"The store free reads and `:store-get` resolve against: while a module\n   148\t   closure runs (`store-of` non-nil), its module store, with no ambient\n   149\t   fallback -- a key the module store lacks is absent; otherwise the\n   150\t   task's own store.\"\n   151\t  [state store-of]\n   152\t  (if (some? store-of)\n   153\t    (get (:module-stores state) store-of {})\n   154\t    (:store state)))\n   155\t\n   156\t\n   157\t(defn put-active\n   158\t  \"Write `key` in the active store of `state`: the module store\n   159\t   `store-of` names, or the task's own store at top level. Both go\n   160\t   through `store-put`, so a reserved key is refused either way.\"\n   161\t  [state store-of key val]\n   162\t  (if (some? store-of)\n   163\t    (update-in state [:module-stores store-of]\n   164\t               (fn [module-store] (store-put (or module-store {}) key val)))\n   165\t    (assoc state :store (store-put (:store state) key val))))\n   166\t\n   167\t\n   168\t(defn- gen-id\n   169\t  \"Generate a unique keyword ID from a prefix and counter value.\"\n   170\t  [prefix id-counter]\n   960\t                           :link-id (:link-id entry)})])))))\n   961\t\n   962\t\n   963\t(defn- poll-link-entry\n   964\t  \"One poll of a link wait entry: a `:link-request` retries its retained\n   965\t   envelope and, appended, polls on as a `:link-response`; an `:install`\n   966\t   waits for its install. Returns `[state waiting woken]`.\"\n   967\t  [state entry]\n   968\t  (case (:reason entry)\n   969\t    :link-request\n   970\t    (let [entry' (module/append-link-request (:resources state) entry)]\n   971\t      (if (= :link-response (:reason entry'))\n   972\t        (poll-link-response state entry')\n   973\t        [state entry' nil]))\n   974\t    :link-response (poll-link-response state entry)\n   975\t    :install [state entry nil]))\n   976\t\n   977\t\n   978\t(defn- poll-links\n   979\t  \"Poll every link wait entry once, in wait-set order, and then step the\n   980\t   install children. Returns the state with the still-waiting link\n   981\t   entries appended to `others` and the woken ones queued.\"\n   982\t  [state links others]\n   983\t  (let [[state waiting woken]\n   984\t        (reduce (fn [[state waiting woken] entry]\n   985\t                  (let [[state w k] (poll-link-entry state entry)]\n   986\t                    [state\n   987\t                     (cond-> waiting w (conj w))\n   988\t                     (cond-> woken k (conj k))]))\n   989\t                [state [] []]\n   990\t                links)]\n   991\t    (-> state\n   992\t        (assoc :wait-set (into (vec others) waiting))\n   993\t        (update :ready-queue (fnil into []) woken)\n   994\t        advance-installs)))\n   995\t\n   996\t\n   997\t(defn abandon-link\n   998\t  \"A composition gives up on link `link-id` (section 7.2, step 7): the\n   999\t   entry leaves the wait set and is restored with `reason` raised as the\n  1000\t   effect's error; the id is retired, so a response arriving later is\n  1001\t   `:late`. The linker side's `abandon` is the composition's call. An id\n  1002\t   no entry holds leaves the state unchanged.\"\n  1003\t  [state link-id reason]\n  1004\t  (let [held? (fn [e]\n  1005\t                (and (contains? #{:link-request :link-response} (:reason e))\n  1006\t                     (= link-id (:link-id e))))]\n  1007\t    (if-let [entry (first (filter held? (:wait-set state)))]\n  1008\t      (-> state\n  1009\t          (update :wait-set (fn [ws] (filterv (complement held?) ws)))\n  1010\t          (retire link-id :abandoned)\n  1011\t          (update :ready-queue (fnil conj [])\n  1012\t                  (refused-entry entry\n  1013\t                                 {:status :lost,\n  1014\t                                  :reason reason,\n  1015\t                                  :link-id link-id})))\n  1016\t      state)))\n  1017\t\n  1018\t\n  1019\t(defn check-wait-set\n  1020\t  \"Check wait-set entries against their transports.\n  1021\t\n  1022\t   The sweep is `dao.stream.waitset/check` — this engine was that library's\n  1023\t   seed and is now its first consumer. Every entry is resolved to a live\n  1024\t   handle and an opaque cursor out of the store by `waitset-resolver` and\n  1025\t   polled with a synchronous `next` or `append!` — resolution happens per\n  1026\t   poll, so the stored entry itself never carries a handle. There is no\n  1027\t   transport-local waking to fall back from: this is the only mechanism.\n  1028\t\n  1029\t   Entries are polled one at a time in wait-set order, and a woken reader's\n  1030\t   successor cursor is written back to the store before the next entry is\n  1031\t   resolved. Waiters sharing a cursor-ref therefore read distinct values —\n  1032\t   the value at the cursor wakes the first, its successor wakes the next —\n  1033\t   instead of every waiter reading the value at the shared pre-poll\n  1034\t   cursor. An entry that stays waiting is retained in its stored,\n  1035\t   resource-id form.\n  1036\t\n  1037\t   Each woken result's `:status` is stamped onto its ready entry, where\n  1038\t   `terminal-resume-outcome` reads it: an outcome the immediate operation\n  1039\t   raises as an error fails the same way when the resume pops it — and a\n  1040\t   waitset diagnostic, an entry the sweep could not poll at all, raises\n  1041\t   there too, before any continuation is restored.\n  1042\t\n  1043\t   The link wait entries `require` adds (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.2) are\n  1044\t   polled first, by the engine rather than the stream sweep: a\n  1045\t   `:link-request` retries its envelope, a `:link-response` advances its\n  1046\t   own kept cursor to the response carrying its id, and an `:install`\n  1047\t   waits on its install child. The install children are then stepped in\n  1048\t   this same round (section 7.3), so a child that halts restores its\n  1049\t   waiters here; nothing about a child runs inside a restore.\"\n  1050\t  [state]\n  1051\t  (let [wait-set (:wait-set state)]\n  1052\t    (if (and (empty? wait-set) (empty? (:installs state)))\n  1053\t      state\n  1054\t      (let [state (poll-links state\n  1055\t                              (filterv link-entry? wait-set)\n  1056\t                              (remove link-entry? wait-set))\n  1057\t            wait-set (:wait-set state)\n  1058\t            streams (filterv (complement link-entry?) wait-set)\n  1059\t            {:keys [woken store], :as result}\n  1060\t            (waitset/check {:waiting streams} waitset-resolver (:store state))\n  1061\t            v (assoc state\n  1062\t                     :store store\n  1063\t                     :wait-set (into (:waiting (:waitset result))\n  1064\t                                     (filter link-entry?)\n  1065\t                                     wait-set))]\n  1066\t        (update v\n  1067\t                :ready-queue (fnil into [])\n  1068\t                (make-woken-run-queue-entries v woken))))))\n  1069\t\n  1070\t\n  1071\t(declare handle-effect resume-continuation)\n  1072\t\n  1073\t\n  1074\t(defn run-loop\n  1075\t  \"Generic eval loop with scheduler support. Ready entries are pure data;\n  1076\t   `resume-fn` pops and restores them.\"\n  1077\t  [state active? step-fn resume-fn]\n  1078\t  (loop [v state]\n  1079\t    (let [q (or (:ready-queue v) [])]\n  1080\t      (cond (active? v) (recur (step-fn v))\n  1235\t                               :halted? false))]\n  1236\t      {:state new-state, :value :yin/blocked, :blocked? true})\n  1237\t    {:state (:state result), :value (:value result), :blocked? false}))\n  1238\t\n  1239\t\n  1240\t(defn handle-effect\n  1241\t  \"Dispatch an effect and return {:state updated-state :value v :blocked? bool}.\n  1242\t   park-entry-fns maps :stream/put and :stream/next to functions that build\n  1243\t   wait entries.\n  1244\t\n  1245\t   A parked entry is stored as the builder left it plus, for a writer, the\n  1246\t   `:datom` it retries: registers and resource ids only. Neither the live\n  1247\t   stream handle nor a restore closure is attached — `check-wait-set`\n  1248\t   resolves handles from the store at every poll, and the scheduler that pops\n  1249\t   a woken entry dispatches restoration itself — so a blocked entry is pure\n  1250\t   data and survives serialization.\"\n  1251\t  [state effect {:keys [park-entry-fns], :as opts}]\n  1252\t  (let [park-entry (get park-entry-fns (:effect effect))\n  1253\t        result\n  1254\t        (case (:effect effect)\n  1255\t          :vm/store-put {:state (put-active state\n  1256\t                                            (store-context state)\n  1257\t                                            (:key effect)\n  1258\t                                            (:val effect)),\n  1259\t                         :value (:val effect),\n  1260\t                         :blocked? false}\n  1261\t          :stream/make\n  1262\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \"stream\")\n  1263\t                [stream-ref new-state] (handle-make s' effect id)]\n  1264\t            {:state new-state, :value stream-ref, :blocked? false})\n  1265\t          :stream/cursor\n  1266\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \"cursor\")\n  1267\t                [cursor-ref new-state] (handle-cursor s' effect id)]\n  1268\t            {:state new-state, :value cursor-ref, :blocked? false})\n  1269\t          :stream/put\n  1270\t          (let [result (handle-put state effect)]\n  1271\t            (if (:park result)\n  1272\t              (let [built-entry (when park-entry\n  1273\t                                  (park-entry state effect result))\n  1274\t                    built-entry (if (and built-entry (not (:datom built-entry)))\n  1275\t                                  (assoc built-entry :datom (:val effect))\n  1276\t                                  built-entry)]\n  1277\t                (handle-stream-block result built-entry))\n  1278\t              {:state (:state result),\n  1279\t               :value (:value result),\n  1280\t               :blocked? false}))\n  1281\t          :stream/next\n  1282\t          (let [result (handle-next state effect)]\n  1283\t            (if (:park result)\n  1284\t              (let [built-entry (when park-entry\n  1285\t                                  (park-entry state effect result))]\n  1286\t                (handle-stream-block result built-entry))\n  1287\t              {:state (:state result),\n  1288\t               :value (:value result),\n  1289\t               :blocked? false}))\n  1290\t          :stream/close\n  1291\t          (let [close-result (handle-close state effect)]\n  1292\t            {:state (:state close-result), :value nil, :blocked? false})\n  1293\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \"effect\")\n  1294\t                handler (module/get-effect-handler (:modules state)\n  1295\t                                                   (:effect effect))]\n  1296\t            (if handler\n  1297\t              (handler s' effect (assoc opts :id id))\n  1298\t              (fail \"Unknown effect\" {:effect (:effect effect)}))))]\n  1299\t    (update result\n  1300\t            :state\n  1301\t            (fn [result-state]\n  1302\t              (telemetry/emit-snapshot (assoc result-state\n  1303\t                                              :value (:value result))\n  1304\t                                       :effect\n  1305\t                                       {:effect-type (:effect effect)})))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc | sed -n '75,180p;285,390p'\"","aggregated_output":"    75\t            images)\n    76\t      (let [[_ off len :as row] (peek images)]\n    77\t        (when (and row (= pc (+ off len))) row))))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(defn continuation-payload\n    81\t  \"Construct a canonical sparse register continuation payload for a\n    82\t   suspending or boundary instruction. Extracts only live registers in\n    83\t   strictly ascending index order.\n    84\t   `runtime` must contain: `:segment`, `:hash`, `:pc`, `:frames`,\n    85\t   `:registers`, and `:continuation`; its offset table `:images` gives\n    86\t   `:image`, the identity of the row the resume pc falls in, which is\n    87\t   what `register-restore` checks (r6).\"\n    88\t  [runtime instruction]\n    89\t  (let [op (first instruction)]\n    90\t    (when-not (boundary-opcodes op)\n    91\t      (throw (ex-info \"Instruction is not a continuation boundary\"\n    92\t                      {:rule :continuation-site, :pc (:pc runtime)})))\n    93\t    (let [site-pc (:pc runtime)\n    94\t          live-idx (rcode/live-slot-index op)\n    95\t          live (nth instruction live-idx)\n    96\t          tail? (and (= :call op) (true? (nth instruction 4)))\n    97\t          dest (if tail? nil (nth instruction 1))\n    98\t          resume-mode (if tail? :return-result :write-result)\n    99\t          regs (mapv (fn [r] [r (nth (:registers runtime) r)]) live)\n   100\t          images (:images runtime)]\n   101\t      (cond-> {:segment (:segment runtime),\n   102\t               :site-pc site-pc,\n   103\t               :pc (inc site-pc),\n   104\t               :frames (:frames runtime),\n   105\t               :regs regs,\n   106\t               :live live,\n   107\t               :continuation (:continuation runtime),\n   108\t               :dest dest,\n   109\t               :resume-mode resume-mode,\n   110\t               :format format-tag,\n   111\t               :hash (:hash runtime),\n   112\t               :image (nth (image-row images (inc site-pc)) 0 nil)}\n   113\t        ;; a code space grown by `attach-image` is a concatenation of\n   114\t        ;; images, each admitted alone: the table travels so each can be\n   115\t        ;; checked alone (`continuation-defect`)\n   116\t        (< 1 (count images)) (assoc :images images)))))\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\t;; =============================================================================\n   120\t;; 3. Continuation payload defect validation (design section 5.2.2)\n   121\t;; =============================================================================\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- nonneg-int?\n   124\t  [x]\n   125\t  (and (integer? x) (not (neg? x))\n   126\t       #?(:cljs (js/Number.isSafeInteger x) :default true)))\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\t(defn- ascending-distinct?\n   130\t  [xs]\n   131\t  (every? (fn [[a b]] (< a b)) (partition 2 1 xs)))\n   132\t\n   133\t\n   134\t(defn- body-of-pc\n   135\t  [{:keys [bodies]} pc]\n   136\t  (some (fn [[i {:keys [start end]}]]\n   137\t          (when (and (<= start pc) (<= pc end)) i))\n   138\t        (map-indexed vector bodies)))\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\t(defn- valid-regs-shape?\n   142\t  [regs]\n   143\t  (and (vector? regs)\n   144\t       (every? (fn [pair]\n   145\t                 (and (vector? pair)\n   146\t                      (= 2 (count pair))\n   147\t                      (nonneg-int? (nth pair 0))))\n   148\t               regs)))\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\t(defn- return-frame-defect\n   152\t  \"The first defect of one return `frame` of a payload whose code space\n   153\t   is `segment`. A frame carries no code space of its own\n   154\t   (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3, r7): its absolute pcs are checked\n   155\t   against the payload's.\"\n   156\t  [segment frame frame-idx]\n   157\t  (if-not (map? frame)\n   158\t    {:rule :continuation-continuation, :frame-index frame-idx}\n   159\t    (let [{:keys [site-pc return-pc frames regs live dest]} frame]\n   160\t      (or (when (not= format-tag (:format frame format-tag))\n   161\t            {:rule :continuation-format, :frame-index frame-idx})\n   162\t          (let [insts (:instructions segment)\n   163\t                len (count insts)]\n   164\t            (or (when-not (and (nonneg-int? site-pc) (< site-pc len))\n   165\t                  {:rule :continuation-pc, :frame-index frame-idx})\n   166\t                (let [inst (nth insts site-pc)\n   167\t                      op (first inst)]\n   168\t                  (or (when-not (= :call op)\n   169\t                        {:rule :continuation-pc, :frame-index frame-idx})\n   170\t                      (when (true? (nth inst 4))\n   171\t                        {:rule :continuation-pc, :frame-index frame-idx})\n   172\t                      (let [body-idx (body-of-pc segment site-pc)\n   173\t                            body (nth (:bodies segment) body-idx)\n   174\t                            call-rd (nth inst 1)\n   175\t                            call-live (nth inst 5)]\n   176\t                        (or (when-not (and (= (inc site-pc) return-pc)\n   177\t                                           (= body-idx\n   178\t                                              (body-of-pc segment return-pc)))\n   179\t                              {:rule :continuation-pc, :frame-index frame-idx})\n   180\t                            (when-not (= call-rd dest)\n   285\t                      {:rule :continuation-pc})\n   286\t                    (let [body-idx (body-of-pc segment site-pc)\n   287\t                          body (nth (:bodies segment) body-idx)\n   288\t                          tail? (and (= :call op) (true? (nth inst 4)))\n   289\t                          expected-mode (if tail? :return-result :write-result)\n   290\t                          inst-live (nth inst (rcode/live-slot-index op))]\n   291\t                      (or (when-not (and (= (inc site-pc) pc)\n   292\t                                         (= body-idx (body-of-pc segment pc)))\n   293\t                            {:rule :continuation-pc})\n   294\t                          (when-not (= expected-mode resume-mode)\n   295\t                            {:rule :continuation-resume-mode})\n   296\t                          (when-not (and (vector? live)\n   297\t                                         (every? nonneg-int? live)\n   298\t                                         (ascending-distinct? live)\n   299\t                                         (every? #(< % (:registers body)) live))\n   300\t                            {:rule :continuation-live})\n   301\t                          (when-not (= inst-live live)\n   302\t                            {:rule :continuation-live,\n   303\t                             :pc site-pc,\n   304\t                             :expected inst-live,\n   305\t                             :actual live})\n   306\t                          (when-not (valid-regs-shape? regs)\n   307\t                            {:rule :continuation-registers})\n   308\t                          (when-not (= live (mapv (fn [p] (nth p 0)) regs))\n   309\t                            {:rule :continuation-registers})\n   310\t                          (when-not (every? (fn [p]\n   311\t                                              (vm/plain-data? (nth p 1)))\n   312\t                                            regs)\n   313\t                            {:rule :continuation-registers})\n   314\t                          (if (= :write-result resume-mode)\n   315\t                            (let [rd (nth inst 1)]\n   316\t                              (or (when-not (= rd dest)\n   317\t                                    {:rule :continuation-destination})\n   318\t                                  (when-not (< dest (:registers body))\n   319\t                                    {:rule :continuation-destination})\n   320\t                                  (when (contains? (set live) dest)\n   321\t                                    {:rule :continuation-destination})))\n   322\t                            (when-not (and (nil? dest) tail?)\n   323\t                              {:rule :continuation-destination}))\n   324\t                          (when-not (and (vector? frames)\n   325\t                                         (every? vector? frames)\n   326\t                                         (vm/plain-data? frames))\n   327\t                            {:rule :continuation-frames})\n   328\t                          (when-not (vector? continuation)\n   329\t                            {:rule :continuation-continuation})\n   330\t                          (some (fn [[idx f]]\n   331\t                                  (return-frame-defect segment f idx))\n   332\t                                (map-indexed vector continuation)))))))))))\n   333\t\n   334\t\n   335\t;; =============================================================================\n   336\t;; 4. Wait-entry defect validation (design section 5.2.3)\n   337\t;; =============================================================================\n   338\t\n   339\t(def ^:private stale-keys\n   340\t  [:value :status :cursor :store-updates :stream\n   341\t   :datom :type :id :request-sent :op])\n   342\t\n   343\t\n   344\t(defn wait-entry-defect\n   345\t  \"Return nil when `entry` is a valid newly parked engine wait-set entry,\n   346\t   or the first deterministic defect map.\n   347\t   Validates the embedded continuation payload and shape-specific transport\n   348\t   fields, and rejects stale wake keys.\"\n   349\t  [entry]\n   350\t  (or (continuation-defect entry)\n   351\t      (let [shape (cond\n   352\t                    (true? (:request-sent entry)) :ffi-writer\n   353\t                    (contains? entry :call-id) :ffi-reader\n   354\t                    (= :put (:reason entry)) :stream-writer\n   355\t                    (= :next (:reason entry)) :stream-reader\n   356\t                    :else nil)]\n   357\t        (if-not shape\n   358\t          {:rule :wait-shape}\n   359\t          (let [prohibited-stale\n   360\t                (case shape\n   361\t                  :ffi-reader stale-keys\n   362\t                  :stream-reader stale-keys\n   363\t                  :stream-writer\n   364\t                  [:value :status :cursor :store-updates :stream\n   365\t                   :type :id :request-sent :op]\n   366\t                  :ffi-writer\n   367\t                  [:value :status :cursor :store-updates :stream\n   368\t                   :type :id])\n   369\t                present-stale (filterv #(contains? entry %) prohibited-stale)]\n   370\t            (or (when (seq present-stale)\n   371\t                  {:rule :wait-stale, :keys present-stale})\n   372\t                (case shape\n   373\t                  :stream-writer\n   374\t                  (or (when-not (keyword? (:stream-id entry))\n   375\t                        {:rule :wait-resource, :field :stream-id})\n   376\t                      (when-not (contains? entry :datom)\n   377\t                        {:rule :wait-resource, :field :datom})\n   378\t                      (when-not (vm/plain-data? (:datom entry))\n   379\t                        {:rule :wait-resource, :field :datom}))\n   380\t\n   381\t                  :stream-reader\n   382\t                  (or (when-not (keyword? (:stream-id entry))\n   383\t                        {:rule :wait-resource, :field :stream-id})\n   384\t                      (let [c (:cursor-ref entry)]\n   385\t                        (when-not (and (map? c)\n   386\t                                       (= :cursor-ref (:type c))\n   387\t                                       (keyword? (:id c)))\n   388\t                        