{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"# M4 S3 commit gate\n\n**Verdict: REJECT.** The orchestrator reports passing JVM, Node, and Dart suites, but the diff does not meet the linker spec’s resource isolation requirements. I did not rerun the suites.\n\n## Findings\n\n- **P0 — Program code can reach engine resources through the task store.** Stream handles and cursor cells are still written into `:store`, and stream effects accept a program supplied reference by its predictable id without a seal check ([engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:254), [engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:277), [engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:297)). The new test proves only that a *module closure* cannot read the parent store; it confirms the live handle remains there ([linker_require_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc:718)). Top level code can read that store, and a literal reference can name an existing resource at effect dispatch. The lift’s refusal of stream and cursor references closes the export path it tests, but does not close these runtime paths. The private resource table and sealed reference checks required by linker r8–r11 are must-fix for this gate.\n\n- **P1 — Install publication can throw instead of refusing the install.** `link-install` catches lift failures, but image attachment, decoding, store lowering, and dependency publication occur outside that catch ([engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:805), [engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:822)). `advance-install` calls `link-install` outside its child-run catch ([engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:853)). A lowering defect can therefore escape the scheduler round while the install and its waiters remain parked, instead of producing the specified refusal.\n\n- **P1 — The register continuation’s image table is insufficiently bound to the code space.** The new validator checks rows individually, but does not require ordered, nonoverlapping, complete coverage of the concatenated instructions; it also accepts any zero-length row without checking its identity ([debruijn_register_effects.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc:233)). The added test checks one forged identity, not missing, overlapping, or reordered rows ([attach_image_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/test/yin/vm/attach_image_test.cljc:364)). The legitimate parked-after-attach case is fixed, but a supplied table can misdescribe which verified images constitute the payload.\n\n## Gate checks\n\n`require` remains an ordinary effect producing function; the changed handler emits a name, format, and contract request and does not itself resolve a name outside the linker’s authority policy ([module.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:411)). The Rule R registry check and its tests address the reserved `yin/def` path and export keys ([vm.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1867), [rule_r_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/test/yin/vm/rule_r_test.cljc:425)). The store-write audit allowlist change follows the move of program writes to `engine/put-active` and does not add a broad exception ([store_write_audit_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj:292)).\n\nThe orchestrator’s ClojureDart fix uses an explicit `:cljd` branch for `runtimeType` ([engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:476)). I found no second comparably clear ClojureDart unsafe form in the changed paths. The report’s deferred `:foreign-image` test leaves that guard unverified: the guard is reached after lift only when a closure origin is absent from the install image and linked registry images ([engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:774), [engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-s3/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:810)); the current tests do not establish its refusal behavior.\n\n**Verdict: REJECT. Must fix:** private resources and sealed reference validation with resource lowering; convert publication and lowering failures into install refusals; validate the register image table’s complete, exact correspondence to the code space."}}
